    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n105038" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τρῐμερ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			<div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>tripartite, threefold,</i>
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἡ φυχή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>VV</u>
					1249a30
				</span></i>
			, cf. <i><span class="en">
				<u>Top.</u>
				133a31
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποταμός</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Agatharch.
					95
				</span></i>
			; of a country, <i><span class="en">
				Str.
				11.2.18
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὧραι</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.S.
					1.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">στάσις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					J.
					<u>BJ</u>
					5.1.1
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φιλοσοφία</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Plu.
					2.874e
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">δρᾶμα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Gal.
				</span></i>
			 in <i><span class="en">
				<u>Abh.Berl.Akad.</u>
				1925(1).38
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">νόμος τ.</span> a piece of music
				<i>in the three modes</i> (Dorian, Phrygian, Lydian), <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				2.1134b
			</span></i> (nisi leg. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριμελής</span>).
				Adv.
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τριμερῶς</span>
			<u>Gloss.</u>
        </div>
